  1	# synthetic-payment-api incident runbook
  2	
  3	## Scope
  4	
  5	This runbook is for read-only investigation of checkout failures. Health is a
  6	liveness signal and is not sufficient evidence that the checkout path is ready.
  7	
  8	## Read-only triage sequence
  9	
 10	1. Check `GET /health` and `GET /metrics`.
 11	2. Check `GET /diagnostics/downstream` and compare it with
 12	   `fixtures/downstream_history.json`.
 13	3. Read `artifacts/runtime/service.jsonl` around the incident window.
 14	4. Compare `fixtures/deployment.json` with the runtime configuration mounted in
 15	   `artifacts/runtime/runtime_config.json`.
 16	5. Test at least two explanations: an application/deployment regression and
 17	   downstream pressure or availability.
 18	
 19	The controller may introduce `GET /diagnostics/timeline` as a fresh
 20	read-only control-plane observation during the second investigation turn. Do
 21	not treat that later observation as part of the initial incident request.
 22	
 23	## Known operating expectations
 24	
 25	- The payment gateway simulator is normally available.
 26	- Normal p95 latency is below 120 ms.
 27	- The checkout timeout budget for the known-safe release is 300 ms.
 28	- A dependency warning means latency exceeded the warning threshold; it does
 29	  not, by itself, prove that the dependency caused checkout failures.
 30	- Do not restart, edit configuration, or deploy during investigation.
 31	
 32	## Remediation boundary
 33	
 34	Only the experiment controller may restore the known-safe configuration. A
 35	human must approve that fixed action before it runs. Afterward, verify health,
 36	checkout behavior, metrics, and new structured logs.
